# .trivyignore
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line, optional trailing comment.
# Entries here are permanently ignored by every trivy image scan in the
# Jenkinsfile until removed.
#
# Process for adding an entry:
# 1. The CVE must have no available fix upstream (Fixed Version: none in
#    the trivy report), OR the fix requires a breaking major-version jump
#    that is tracked as separate, deliberate work (not silently ignored).
# 2. Add an expiry date in the comment — 90 days out — and revisit before
#    then. An unfixable-today CVE may become fixable in that window.
# 3. Only the project owner adds entries here; this file is not a place
#    to silence CI failures under time pressure without justification.
#
# Currently empty — no CVE has been evaluated as unfixable yet.
